<div class="govuk-main-wrapper ">

    <div class="govuk-grid-row">
        <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
            <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Accessibility statement  for the Data Marketplace</h1>
            <p class="govuk-body">The Data Marketplace is committed to making its website accessible, in accordance with the Public Sector Bodies (Websites and Mobile Applications) (No. 2) Accessibility Regulations 2018.</p>
            <p class="govuk-body">This accessibility statement applies to the Data Marketplace website at: <a class="govuk-link" href="https://datamarketplace.gov.uk">https://datamarketplace.gov.uk</a>.</p>
            <p class="govuk-body">This page explains how accessible this website is, the improvements we’ve made and how to report accessibility problems.</p>
            <p class="govuk-body">There is a separate <a class="govuk-link" rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.gov.uk/help/accessibility-statement">accessibility statement for the main GOV.UK website (opens in new tab)</a>.</p>
            
            <h1 class="govuk-heading-l">Using this service</h1>
            <p class="govuk-body">This service is run by the Department for Science, Innovation and Technology (DSIT). We want as many people as possible to be able to use this service.</p>
            <p class="govuk-body">You should be able to:</p>
            <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
                <li>zoom in up to 200% without the text spilling off the screen</li>
                <li>navigate the website using just a keyboard</li>
                <li>navigate the website using speech recognition software</li>
                <li>use the website with a screen reader – including JAWS, NVDA and VoiceOver</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="govuk-body">We’ve also made the text in the service as simple as possible to understand.</p>
            <p class="govuk-body">The service is currently in private beta and subject to ongoing user research and testing, including accessibility audits.</p>
            
            <h1 class="govuk-heading-l">Compliance status</h1>
            <p class="govuk-body">The service fully complies with WCAG 2.1 AA standards and incorporates improvements recommended for WCAG 2.2.</p>

            <h1 class="govuk-heading-l">Improvements we’ve made</h1>
            <p class="govuk-body">In summer 2024 the Digital Accessibility Centre (DAC) conducted an accessibility audit of the Data Marketplace. </p>
            <p class="govuk-body">This identified several issues which we’ve now resolved, including:</p>
            <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
                <li>form controls – all form controls now have meaningful names and logical structures for screen readers</li>
                <li>skip links – ’skip to main content’ links allow keyboard-only users to bypass repetitive elements</li>
                <li>screen reader feedback – buttons, links and pagination controls now have clear, descriptive labels</li>
                <li>text resizing and reflow – the website supports resizing up to 200% without loss of functionality, meeting reflow requirements</li>
                <li>heading structure – logical hierarchies across pages improve screen reader navigation</li>
                <li>fieldset grouping – related form controls are grouped with proper fieldset and legend tags</li>
                <li>pagination labels – pagination controls are labelled descriptively for better usability</li>
                <li>visible input labels – all input fields now have clear, visible labels</li>
                <li>distinct links – duplicate links now have unique identifiers for screen readers, for example on the Manage Organisations page</li>
            </ul>
            
            <h1 class="govuk-heading-l">Reporting accessibility problems with this website</h1>
            <p class="govuk-body">If you find any problems that are not listed on this page or you think we’re not meeting the accessibility requirements, email us at: <a class="govuk-link" href="mailto:datamarketplace@digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk">datamarketplace@digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk</a>.</p>
            <p class="govuk-body">It will help if you include:</p>
            <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
                <li>your name</li>
                <li>the URL of the page you want to tell us about (if relevant)</li>
            </ul>
            
            <h1 class="govuk-heading-l">Enforcement procedure</h1>
            <p class="govuk-body">The Equality and Human Rights Commission (EHRC) is responsible for enforcing the Public Sector Bodies (Websites and Mobile Applications) (No. 2) Accessibility Regulations 2018 (the ‘accessibility regulations’).</p>
            <p class="govuk-body">If you’re not happy with how we respond to your complaint, <a class="govuk-link" rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.equalityadvisoryservice.com/">contact the Equality Advisory and Support Service (opens in new tab)</a>, which is run on behalf of EHRC.</p>

            <h1 class="govuk-heading-l">Preparation of this accessibility statement</h1>
            <p class="govuk-body">This statement was prepared on 27 September 2023. It was last updated on 28 February 2025.</p>
            <p class="govuk-body">It is based on:</p>
            <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
                <li>the findings and recommendations of the summer 2024 DAC audit</li>
                <li>remediation work completed between summer and winter 2024</li>
                <li>continuous accessibility testing and feedback</li>
            </ul>

            <p class="govuk-body">Last updated 28 February 2025</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>